cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use HAMLET in research, please cite the associated IEEE Robotics and
  Automation Letters (RA-L) paper using the bibliographic reference specified
  in the Zenodo archival record linked in README.md, under "How to cite the
  software". Also identify the software version and its archival record.
  The software metadata below does not replace the requested paper citation.
type: software
title: "HAMLET: Hand Anthropometric Measurement and Landmark Extraction Tool"
version: "1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JonAndoniFdez/HAMLET"
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  Desktop application for hand anthropometry from textured 3D flat-hand models,
  with anatomical landmark detection, interactive review and measurement export.
  GPL-3.0-only applies to original HAMLET code; bundled third-party components
  and OpenPose models retain their own terms.
